# Line endings: the launcher scripts are bash and the JSON/JS are parsed as
# text, so a Windows checkout must not rewrite them to CRLF (a `#!/bin/bash\r`
# shebang and a CRLF JSON file both fail in ways that are hard to diagnose).
# Git's own executable-bit support is what carries the 100755 modes; Windows
# checkouts additionally need `core.filemode=true` over a WSL mount.
*.sh text eol=lf
*.mjs text eol=lf
*.js text eol=lf
*.json text eol=lf
*.yml text eol=lf
*.md text eol=lf

# No text conversion for anything binary that might be added later.
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.gz binary
